{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnRMLvvib3ntzkGjo5Ns","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 1 showed the architecture. There are 18 layers with hidden size 640 and 4 query heads sharing 1 KV head of dim 256. The MLP has 2048 units (GeGLU). Layers 5, 11 and 17 use global attention and the rest are sliding-window. The configs are identical. Still p(A) = 0.5.\n\nNext I measure, for every tensor, three things:\n- the fraction of entries that differ between A and B in bf16;\n- the relative Frobenius norm of A−B;\n- the effective rank of A−B (from its singular values).\n\nA low-rank difference would suggest LoRA, which would let me think about decomposing the two deltas. A sparse difference, where only some entries change, matters too. Entries where A == B are likely still equal to the base model. Entries where only one model moved might then let me reconstruct the base and attribute each change to A or B. This step is symmetric in A and B.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\nrows=[]\nfor k in A.keys():\n    a=A.get(k); b=B.get(k); d=a-b\n    frac=(d!=0).mean()\n    rel=np.linalg.norm(d)/ (np.linalg.norm(a)+1e-12)\n    r=\"\"\n    if d.ndim==2:\n        s=np.linalg.svd(d,compute_uv=False)\n        e=(s**2)/ (s**2).sum()\n        cum=np.cumsum(e)\n        r=f\"top1={e[0]:.3f} k90={np.searchsorted(cum,0.9)+1} s0={s[0]:.4f}\"\n    rows.append((k,frac,rel,np.linalg.norm(d),r))\nfor k,frac,rel,n,r in rows:\n    print(f\"{k:55s} frac={frac:.3f} rel={rel:.5f} norm={n:.4f} {r}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3447,"cache_read_input_tokens":2858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3447},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_managem